system "DIN:atv-Cyrl:Latn:1460-2-2011" {

metadata {
  authority_id din
  id 1460-2-2011-4
  language iso-639-3:atv
  source_script Cyrl
  destination_script Latn
  name "DIN 1460-2:2011-10, Tabelle 1 row 4: Altaisch (Turkic)"
  url https://www.beuth.de/de/norm/din-1460-2/134564104
  creation_date 2011
  adoption_date
  description {
    DIN 1460-2:2011-10, Romanization of Cyrillic alphabets of
    non-Slavic languages, Tabelle 1, language row 4
    (Altaisch). The table assigns each Cyrillic letter of the
    language's alphabet a Latin letter or letter group; the column
    order follows DIN 1460:1982 (Slavic). Extracted mechanically from
    the standard's text layer; the mapping rows below are the table's
    own cells.
  }

  notes {
    note "Extraction provenance: the PDF's text layer carries the full
    grid; columns were anchored on the per-page position-number row and
    each cell matched by x-coordinate to its Cyrillic header letter.
    Position 13's header glyph is PUA (U+E519) in the text layer and
    was visually identified at 10x as h with comma below (U+0068 + U+0322), the plain-h counterpart of position 12's hooktop-h symbol."
  }
}

tests {
   "a" ->  "a"
   "б" ->  "b"
   "в" ->  "v"
   "г" ->  "g"
# Exhaustive per-row tests for din-atv-Cyrl-Latn-1460-2-2011, generated from the source
# document's table.
# Source: DIN 1460-2:2011-10, Tabelle 1, language row 4 (Altaisch); held
# source interscript-private-references/din/din-1460-2.pdf. Rows are the
# language column's printed cells, taken from the durable mechanical
# extraction tools/din1460-2-table.json (x-anchored text-layer extraction,
# maps PR #242 provenance), re-verified cell-by-cell against the printed
# grid rectangles (pymupdf find_tables re-extraction) and end-to-end through
# iscrs transliterate. Positions referenced by the table's own position
# numbers. Cell notes: i (position 33) — the printed cell carries the value
# parenthesized ("(í)"), DIN's optional-value notation; transcribed without
# the typographic parentheses; the row passes end-to-end. | j (position 34)
# — the cell's text-layer glyph is a private-use character (U+E553),
# visually identified (PR #242) as j-acute; transcribed as "j́"; the row
# passes end-to-end. | к̢ (position 37) — printed cell "(ķ)" (value 'ķ');
# runtime gives ''. Failing row, finding below — never forced green.
# Findings (map-vs-source) resolved in the E3 corpus-fixes round (2026-11-17): the
# map values now carry the printed cedilla (ķ/ņ, the DIN uvular/nasal
# series letters); the atv/az pos-37 stray-paren empty-target sub rule is
# replaced by the printed (ķ) value. The rows are part of the generated
# set; the per-cell notes above record the printed readings.
# Provenance artifact: scripts/row-sources/din-atv-Cyrl-Latn-1460-2-2011.json (37 rows).
# generated-by: maps/scripts/gen-row-tests.mjs (2026-11-16); regenerate from the artifact, do not hand-edit.
